  "original_design_criterion_verbatim": "SEPARATE if eps_rec(N-body), eps_rec(SPH alpha=0) <= 1e-8 R and shrink under dt-halving while eps_rec(SPH alpha=1) >= 1e-3 R and does not, with min S_dot_visc >= 0 and ledger closure <= 1e-3; SAME if all three within 10x; growth above 1e-8 that halves with dt is Lyapunov, not irreversibility. S8 sentinel: sum m u_int(T) = Q_cum(T) to 1e-3 and K + W_soft + U_int conserved to 1e-4.",
  "evaluation_point": "primary verdict at T = 1 t_ff (the X2 trimmed design); T = 0.3 t_ff reported alongside",
  "design_corrections_identified_before_running": [
   "C1 'shrink under dt-halving' is wrong for the Hamiltonian engines: velocity-Verlet with position-only forces is exactly time-symmetric, so the echo error is roundoff x chaotic amplification, not truncation. Halving dt doubles the roundoff injections and leaves the amplification unchanged; expected ratio eps(dt/2)/eps(dt) ~ 1-2, not < 1. The original criterion therefore cannot return SEPARATE whatever the physics. Corrected discriminator below (perturbation-size control).",
   "C2 'ledger closure' against the softened mechanical energy K + U_soft: with eos='isothermal' the PdV work also goes to the bath, so the closure only holds if the mechanical energy includes the isothermal free energy F = c_s^2 sum m ln rho. Literal closure (K + U_soft only) reported too; predicted to fail for alpha=1 (density field does not return).",
   "C3 S8 sentinel 'sum m u_int(T) = Q_cum(T)': for eos='isothermal' u_int == 0 by design (work goes to scene.energy_bath_J); for eos='ideal' Delta U_int = Q_visc + W_PdV, not Q_visc alone. Literal sentinel predicted to FAIL for both EOS for this reason, not for an engine defect. Corrected sentinel: |Delta(K + U_soft + U_int + bath)| / |U_soft(0)| <= 1e-4, and the engine's own viscous share (pair-decomposed) equals the independent ledger Q_led to 1e-3 at dt = t_ff/1200.",
   "C4 min S_dot_visc >= 0 holds by construction (Pi_ij > 0 only for approaching pairs; cubic-spline W' <= 0), as does the Fourier face-by-face k dT^2/(Ta Tb) >= 0: engine validation, not evidence.",
   "C5 Reversibility of N-body and inviscid SPH follows from the symplectic integrator and position-only forces; it holds for any force law and any constants. SEPARATE is engine validation of where the closure terms were put, not evidence about the unification thesis."
  ],
  "corrected_criterion": {
   "SEPARATE": [
    "H1: eps_rec(N-body) and eps_rec(SPH alpha=0, isothermal) <= 1e-8 R at both dt, OR above 1e-8 R but linear in an injected displacement delta (log-slope in [0.7, 1.3] over delta points with 3 eps_rec(0) <= eps_rec(delta) <= 1e-2 R) = Lyapunov",
    "H2: Hamiltonian eps_rec is dt-independent at roundoff: eps(dt/2)/eps(dt) in [0.1, 10]",
    "D1: eps_rec(SPH alpha=1) >= 1e-3 R at both dt AND dt-converged |eps(dt/2)/eps(dt) - 1| <= 0.1 AND delta-independent |eps(delta=1e-9 R)/eps(0) - 1| <= 0.1",
    "D2: min S_dot_led >= 0 every step (by construction) and engine per-step viscous booking q_visc >= 0 every step",
    "D3: corrected ledger closure |Q_led - (-Delta(K + U_soft + F))| / Q_led <= 1e-3 at dt = t_ff/1200"
   ],
   "SAME": "all three eps_rec within 10x of each other AND the Hamiltonian echo errors are delta-independent (genuine loss)",
